<title>RUSSIA: TABLE-ROSTELEKOM H1 97 NET FALLS TO 431 BLN RBLS.</title>
<headline>TABLE-ROSTELEKOM H1 97 NET FALLS TO 431 BLN RBLS.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p> (bln rbls)			  1997		   1996</p>
<p> Revenues			   3,731.2		3,184.2</p>
<p> Costs				2,296.2		1,608.6</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit		   1,202.3		1,378.3</p>
<p> Net profit			   431.2		  585.5</p>
<p>NOTES -- Full company name is AOOT Mezhdugorodnoi i Mezhdunarodnoi Elektricheskoi Svyazi Rostelekom .</p>
<p>Telecoms holding company Svyazinvest owns a controlling 38 percent stake in Rostelekom.</p>
<p>These figures are not prepared to international accounting standards but to Russian accounting standards on an accruals basis. Russian accounts are designed to meet the requirements of the tax authorities, and converting Russian accounts to international standards can turn a profit into a loss.</p>
<p>--Olga Popova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
